# .spun get by the alias @ALIAS@, which the server resolves to als001. The
# reply names the real id, so .spun offers als001's suggested directory, y
# installs it, and spun.cat gets als001, never the alias. The second get by
# the alias checks spun.cat with the real id, so it asks "Install again?"
# and not for a directory; n ends it. mame-alias.sh checks spun.cat and the
# installed file after the run.
put @SPUN@ /dot/SPUN
autostart .spun get @ALIAS@
autostart .spun get @ALIAS@
autostart PRINT "SPUNALIASDONE"
autostart FOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0: NEXT i
seconds 35
noreset 7.5
key 16 y
key 25 n
snap 15 20 24 28 34
screen 34 Alias Test A
screen 34 Install to C:/apps/alsa? (y/n) y
screen 34 Installed. Install again? (y/n)
screen 34 SPUNALIASDONE
